1788735426080374	edict-dev	itc:v3:AWLkkmTOfzk5kQAAAAAAQeqtbv7rtAAAAAEvYA		item.create	bn-2jdv	{"description":"Context: the author agent already knows the Seal review id and Maw workspace at review creation time; a dedicated reviewer must receive those authoritative values rather than discover pending work. Goal: add managed workflow documents that define the author launch procedure and the one-review Codex Daybreak contract. Approach: add a security-review workflow document; update review-request, review-response, worker-loop, finish/merge guidance, README and AGENTS templates. The recipe must use a unique labeled Vessel session, canonical <project>-security Seal identity, review:// claim, exact workspace cwd, gpt-daybreak-blue-latest, submit-before-wait timestamp, agentbus PID completion, anchored Rite verdict, Seal vote verification, re-review freshness, and risk high/critical behavior. It must prohibit source edits, commits, merges, pushes, ambient review discovery, and approval inferred from model prose. Acceptance: no managed documentation directs @<project>-security; all referenced commands are valid against current Vessel, Agentbus, Seal, Rite and Maw help; one review contract is complete enough for a fresh agent to execute.","kind":"task","labels":["security-review","docs","daybreak"],"parent":"bn-cae8","size":"m","title":"Define the direct Daybreak security-review launch and reviewer contracts"}	blake3:r6UvoruV5FTo5QwVmwniHlUsA0OPPFjJUljf-jZ6ZCE
1788735434056761	edict-dev	itc:v3:AWLkkmTOfzk5kQAAAAAAQeqtbv7rtAAAAAEvYQ		item.create	bn-x963	{"description":"Context: automatic @<project>-security hooks launch reviewer-loop, which runs an ambient workspace scan and invokes Pi/Claude. Goal: remove this competing path while retaining Seal reviewer assignments and approval gates. Approach: delete reviewer-loop command/config/templates and init/hook registration; add an idempotent sync migration that removes only Edict-owned named reviewer hooks (never user-owned hooks); update hook health checks, schema/config rendering, migration tests, command help/evals and generated-file versions. Acceptance: edict init/sync no longer creates reviewer mention hooks; an existing named edict:<project>:reviewer-security hook is retired once; user-owned hooks survive; reviewer-loop is absent from the public command surface; no production path routes Daybreak through Pi.","kind":"task","labels":["security-review","migration","hooks"],"parent":"bn-cae8","size":"m","title":"Retire security reviewer loop, configuration, and Edict-owned mention hooks"}	blake3:1N0om7xply6NBPgcR0PzRoVP0YlwwhIKc_SRLKU5xN4
1788735439871741	edict-dev	itc:v3:AWLkkmTOfzk5kQAAAAAAQeqtbv7rtAAAAAEvYg		item.create	bn-235r	{"description":"Context: the replacement must demonstrate real protocol safety rather than merely document a model choice. Goal: add focused unit/integration coverage for rendered direct-review docs, hook retirement migration, and direct-session lifecycle semantics. Approach: use isolated Rite data and fake/fixture command paths where needed to assert multiple pending reviews do not alter the explicit target, stale/review-workspace mismatches fail, duplicate review claims fail, Agentbus blocked/timeout/unavailable states produce no approval, anchored verdicts remain required, and re-review needs a fresh Seal vote. Acceptance: tests distinguish submit-before-wait watermark from stale results; cargo test plus format/clippy pass; docs and generated hashes are current.","kind":"task","labels":["security-review","testing","agentbus"],"parent":"bn-cae8","size":"m","title":"Prove exact-target Daybreak review dispatch and failure gates"}	blake3:cmeQG0a2XFkXgwHrDcnIfQhgoXlAdM0eWGa4OkF3794
