1790470566716258	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3cud	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:YNU-pkEYrcCN92TR6Wg6qKxkIjdKOBneod7IkRkGBq0
1790470566883098	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-in11	{"description":"Add an integration test that runs 'edict init --no-interactive' then 'edict sync' against a tempdir project with RITE_DATA_DIR=<tempdir>/rite and HOME pointed at a tempdir. Assert: hooks land in the sandbox data dir; nothing is written under the real data dir (use a sentinel HOME so a leak is detectable). Audit every rite/vessel/seal/maw subprocess edict spawns (src/subprocess.rs Tool, ensure_rite_hook) for env scrubbing (env_clear/env_remove) that would drop RITE_DATA_DIR, and fix any. Skip gracefully if rite is not installed.","kind":"task","labels":["rite"],"parent":"bn-3cud","size":"s","title":"Hermetic test: init and sync register rite hooks only in RITE_DATA_DIR"}	blake3:Uy4_3PMfFokDwXVuEW29v0r7AVBERFU07dNtT0E38ks
1790470567051140	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1lgf	{"description":"Render every managed component and list what would change (files created/updated, migrations to run, rite hooks to add/adopt/rewrite with name, channel, cwd, command), then exit 0 without writing anything or invoking mutating subprocesses. Distinct from --check (which only answers stale/not stale).\n\nAcceptance:\n- Mutating subprocess calls go through one choke point that the dry-run mode short-circuits (no ad-hoc if-dry-run sprinkled per call site).\n- Test: dry-run on a stale project leaves the tree and the sandbox rite data dir byte-identical, and its output lists the pending changes.\n- --help text and cli-conventions compliance (src/templates/design/cli-conventions.md dry-run section).","kind":"task","labels":["cli"],"parent":"bn-3cud","size":"m","title":"Add 'edict sync --dry-run': report planned file writes and hook changes without executing them"}	blake3:Y1aELD9ng9oCCDcfOKk6eeqdJZd3rNwxOXtrfhAHL6I
1790470567210780	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3n53	{"description":"init writes .agents/edict, AGENTS.md, .edict.toml, runs bn/maw/seal init, registers hooks, seeds bones and commits. --dry-run prints each of those as planned actions and performs none. Reuse the choke point from the sync dry-run bone.\n\nAcceptance: test asserting a dry-run init on an empty tempdir leaves it empty and leaves the sandbox rite data dir untouched, with output listing the planned hooks.","kind":"task","labels":["cli"],"parent":"bn-3cud","size":"s","title":"Add 'edict init --dry-run' reusing the sync dry-run machinery"}	blake3:gSBLQm4s8JkNhpB5OWyGKYXjJz96rRDBEatVkQjUyFQ
1790470567362816	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-lq0r	{"description":"Before ensure_rite_hook mutates anything, print the resolved rite data dir (RITE_DATA_DIR or default) and each hook's name/channel/cwd. If the project root is under the system temp dir and RITE_DATA_DIR is unset, refuse hook registration with an error naming RITE_DATA_DIR and --dry-run, unless an explicit --allow-live-hooks flag is given.\n\nAcceptance: unit test for the temp-dir guard; integration test that init in a tempdir without RITE_DATA_DIR registers no hooks and exits with the guidance message.","kind":"task","labels":["rite"],"parent":"bn-3cud","size":"s","title":"Announce rite data dir and each hook before registering; warn for temp-dir projects"}	blake3:WsLVYnlECBtZEf-HtW6NCqWuE4fpOHWc9KcYk2c35I8
1790470567505435	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-31k2	{"description":"Add a 'Testing template changes safely' section to AGENTS.md (and the managed template if agents in downstream projects need it): use --dry-run to preview, or RITE_DATA_DIR=$(mktemp -d) plus a throwaway project for a full run; how to confirm the live hook set is untouched (rite hooks list count). Run edict sync so the managed copy matches.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-3cud","size":"xs","title":"Document the sandbox recipe for testing template changes (AGENTS.md + managed docs)"}	blake3:qQDx5Y6hUbJtWLJageGnQyr_4S5pmoxclK1LzMw-KDE
