1790541312673184	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-30a0	{"description":"The managed section is about 385 lines / 3,100 words / 5k tokens, loaded into every agent context in 19 projects. About 1,100 words are command tables that the tools' own help covers (bn tldr, rite tldr, maw/seal --help). About 450 words are STE and reply-style rules tuned for Opus 5; the user asked to drop them. About 1,300 words are cross-tool policy that no --help teaches.\n\nTarget shape: a one-line pointer per tool (bones: `bn tldr`, rite: `rite tldr`, maw and seal: --help, edict protocol --help); a short Rules list (track work in a bone; edit only in a maw workspace; never merge or destroy default; conflicts are a normal state; run maw ws recover before concluding work is lost; reviewed work merges only via edict protocol merge; run the edict protocol command at each transition; rite reply anchoring, ask-and-wait, never re-send; seal completion is not approval); one rite message-shape rule; the workflow-doc index. Detailed review and merge sequences live in the workflow docs and protocol output, not the managed section. Drop the STE Language rules and the 'Replies to a human' rules.\n\nRisk: many rules were added after real failures (for example the rite wait --mention error that reached 15 repos). Every removed rule must be shown enforced elsewhere, and an A/B eval must show no regression.\n\nExit gate (manual):\n1. Rendered managed section is at most about 1,500 tokens, and a test enforces the budget.\n2. The enforcement audit shows every removed rule is covered elsewhere or deliberately dropped.\n3. The A/B eval (current vs trimmed) shows no regression on the agent-loop, R4 and R6 scenarios.\n4. Released and synced downstream.\n5. A human reads the new section and one downstream AGENTS.md and signs off.","kind":"goal","labels":["goal:manual","docs"],"size":"xl","title":"Trim the edict-managed AGENTS.md section to rules + tool pointers"}	blake3:YXv0v5VZt86zbS1VW3MoJI9LlmVkpQsoDz6vijCAtb4
1790541313143695	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-97do	{"description":"For every rule or instruction in src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja, record where else it is enforced or taught:\n- edict protocol command output (src/commands/protocol/*)\n- loop prompts (src/commands/dev_loop/prompt.rs, worker_loop.rs, responder.rs, src/reply.rs)\n- tool errors or refusals (for example: does maw refuse to merge or destroy default? does seal mark-merged exit 1 on a stale approval?)\n- a workflow doc (.agents/edict/*.md)\n\nVerify tool behavior from help, source, or a sandboxed run (AGENTS.md 'Testing template changes safely'), not from memory.\n\nOutput: notes/managed-trim-audit.md, a table with columns rule | keep in managed section, or covered by <where>, or drop (why). A rule enforced nowhere else either stays in the Rules list or moves into a workflow doc (next bone).\n\nAlso record where a tool's help contradicts edict policy. Known case: maw --help quick start says --from origin/main and 'maw ws merge ... --into default' with no --destroy, --message or review gate.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Audit: where is each managed-section rule enforced besides AGENTS.md?"}	blake3:BR3dVdCpW2GXlZxr8HAep6ue8jKXtVUTZ_UUBPIIh48
1790541313607246	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ox9	{"description":"Using the audit, make sure everything the trimmed section drops lives in a workflow doc or in protocol output:\n- the LGTM, review-log and mark-merged sequence and the uncommitted-changes check (merge-check.md, finish.md)\n- retarget before re-request, and review range semantics (review-request.md, review-response.md)\n- agentbus completion is not approval, and dedicated reviewer reply rules (security-review.md)\n- the threads and ask-and-wait exit-code table, and cross-project tracking bones (cross-channel.md)\n\nKeep one source of truth per rule. Link rather than duplicate.\n\nAcceptance: every 'covered by workflow doc' row in the audit points at real text. The template render-parity tests and the retarget regression test in src/template.rs pass. The rendered .agents/edict copies are regenerated.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Move detailed review/merge/rite sequences out of the managed section into workflow docs"}	blake3:4vlj2EhCF6WJbqi6RzHGYDEbfN-X72vsWhEAH9ozI6s
1790541313863441	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-21zp	{"description":"Rewrite src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja to the goal's target shape.\n\nRemove: the Bones, Workspace and Protocol quick-reference tables; the Bus Communication table; the Claims snippet; the directory tree (replace with one or two layout-aware lines, keeping root vs bare handling); the Reviews and LGTM detail (now in workflow docs); the STE Communication and Language rules; 'Replies to a human'.\n\nKeep: tool pointers (bn tldr, rite tldr, maw --help, seal --help, edict protocol --help); the Rules list; one rite message-shape rule (one or two lines, lead with the label subject, anchor with --reply-to); release instructions and the project-specific blocks the template renders conditionally; the workflow-doc index.\n\nAcceptance: renders for both layouts and all tool combinations (bones, maw, seal, rite, vessel toggles) with no dangling references. Existing template tests updated. This repo's AGENTS.md managed block is re-rendered without a live edict sync (use the sandbox recipe or a render helper). Rendered section is at most about 1,500 tokens.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"m","title":"Rewrite agents-managed.md.jinja to the rules + pointers shape"}	blake3:qhLYJ8W4Jak_ZQXaPCvHVUbBDtbLXbzOjnUQwZ0i0QU
1790541314145755	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-18cq	{"description":"Add a template test that renders the managed section for the largest tool and layout combination and fails if it exceeds a word budget. Set the budget from the trimmed draft (about 1,100 words, about 1,500 tokens). Add a short comment that explains the budget and how to raise it deliberately. This keeps the section from creeping back.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"xs","title":"Test: managed-section size budget"}	blake3:-CYvvgIZUSJQxMe_tCVdwKO-4P1o_GGB4PnhvsMrWNM
1790541314406479	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-19jd	{"description":"Search src/ (loop prompts, protocol output, reply.rs), src/templates/docs/*.md, README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md for references to headings or content that the rewrite removes (for example 'Bones Quick Reference', 'Workspace Quick Reference', 'Communication', STE). Point them at the tool help or the workflow doc instead.\n\nAcceptance: no reference to a removed heading remains. If cheap, add a test that rendered docs and prompts do not mention removed headings.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Fix references to removed managed-section headings in prompts and docs"}	blake3:Ru3TybcM5Owm7Xyjb_LmAvr1-qfPX8SqZqdXbXjkXWs
1790541314658651	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1oug	{"description":"evals/scripts and evals/rubrics.md date from January and February 2026 and use old names (crit for seal, botbox for edict, beads for bones) and old commands. Update the agent-loop, R4 (worker + review + merge) and R6 (lead dispatch) scenarios to run against current bn, maw, seal, rite, vessel and edict 0.31 or later.\n\nEvery run must be hermetic per AGENTS.md 'Testing template changes safely': RITE_DATA_DIR, HOME and XDG_* in a tempdir, AGENT variables unset. Check that the live 'rite hooks list' count is unchanged after a run.\n\nMake the managed-section variant selectable (for example a flag or env var pointing at an alternate template or AGENTS.md) so the A/B can run both.\n\nAcceptance: one smoke run of each scenario completes and scores against its rubric.","kind":"task","labels":["evals"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"m","title":"Bring the evals harness up to date with current tools"}	blake3:6MUfwfinUG46eBrTny2xH5nAvwByZdjwE478-NvOlG0
1790541314952479	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-25zp	{"description":"Run each scenario at least 3 times with the CURRENT managed section. Use models that match real use (for example a Sonnet worker and an Opus lead). Record scores, tool-call counts and failure notes in evals/results/<date>-managed-baseline-*.md. Note context token usage if available.","kind":"task","labels":["evals"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"m","title":"Eval baseline: current managed section on agent-loop, R4, R6"}	blake3:Gr84kZpdsBsuigoHGE_ybb2r1io8DsC-Y9AOQu66Q4Q
1790541315214123	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1kp6	{"description":"Rerun the same scenarios, models and run count with the trimmed section. Compare scores, failure modes and tool-call counts. Some extra --help or tldr calls are expected and fine; a wrong action is not.\n\nFor any regression traced to a removed rule, restore that rule to the Rules list (or fix the covering doc or protocol output) and rerun the affected scenario.\n\nRecord results in evals/results/<date>-managed-trimmed-*.md and add a short verdict comment on the goal.","kind":"task","labels":["evals"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"m","title":"Eval A/B: trimmed managed section vs baseline"}	blake3:nFsqHud17mkcPKRp4SIh-M7-GRf6XIp1UpNRCaTks1g
1790541315448032	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-10fm	{"description":"The unmanaged top half of this repo's AGENTS.md (the Tool Quick Reference: rite, maw, seal, bones and vessel command lists, roughly lines 100 to 230) repeats what the tools' help and the managed section cover. Keep edict-developer content: the spawn chain, hook convergence, the Effects and dry-run notes, the testing recipe, the architecture. Replace generic tool command lists with pointers. Keep facts that agents developing edict rely on (for example the rite wait exit codes, if not documented elsewhere).","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Trim duplicated tool references from edict's own unmanaged AGENTS.md"}	blake3:IUPSGTJZ0dJzRFSSGIvOssqRYcawn7_q0Yodm7Ys8zo
1790541315690305	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3pto	{"description":"maw --help QUICK START and WORKFLOW say 'maw ws create <name> --from origin/main' and 'maw ws merge <name1> <name2> --into default', with no --destroy and no --message, and merge actually requires --message when not interactive. An agent pointed only at maw --help follows that recipe.\n\nAsk on #maw (anchored rite send plus rite wait, per cross-channel.md) and/or create a bone in the maw repo. Propose a quick start that matches current flags and says that an orchestrator such as edict may gate merges. Record the anchor here.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"xs","title":"File maw issue: --help quick start contradicts the edict merge workflow"}	blake3:Y-16JdY-17l1krnXVYFFns7vNBloIKB74fMYs5qjxKo
1790541315935805	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-26zg	{"description":"Bump the version and update CHANGELOG (describe the trim and the dropped STE rules). Release via maw release, then just install. Preview every downstream project with 'edict sync --dry-run' before the real sync; expect only the AGENTS.md managed block to shrink. Confirm the live rite hook count is unchanged.","kind":"task","labels":["release"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Release the trimmed managed section and sync downstream"}	blake3:--qnbMeGR7UogjwyWMUSIRq1paRv7q-SbSbdHtZsq5I
