1790555707892815	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2cf9	{"description":"Found by the managed-section audit (notes/managed-trim-audit.md). The managed section and security-review.md forbid an `@<project>-security` mention (the ambient hook is retired; security review is a dedicated Daybreak launch per security-review.md). src/commands/protocol/review.rs still emits it (around L215-221, L385-390, L452).\n\nFix: emit the security-review.md launch contract steps (request anchor + dedicated launch) instead of the mention. Tests: protocol review output for a project with the security reviewer contains no `@...-security` mention and does contain the launch-contract pointer.","kind":"bug","labels":["review"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"edict protocol review still emits the retired @<project>-security mention"}	blake3:j__pJ4p6ti7Ld3EbNI_C-BxnJlLiDWbzjPUZtIrojE4
1790555708073467	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-30vn	{"description":"Found by the managed-section audit. The managed section says: no work is ever lost in maw; always run `maw ws recover` before concluding work was lost or starting over. Three places teach the opposite: the dev-loop prompt (src/commands/dev_loop/prompt.rs), the worker prompt (src/commands/worker_loop.rs), and src/templates/docs/worker-loop.md around L44.\n\nFix all three to check `maw ws recover <ws>` first and restore with `--to <new-name>` before recreating. Regenerate .agents/edict copies. Test: the rendered docs and built prompts mention `maw ws recover` wherever they describe a missing/destroyed workspace.","kind":"bug","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Prompts and worker-loop.md tell agents to recreate a destroyed workspace from scratch without maw ws recover"}	blake3:L94qnYaCTPRbOC94GRpyZRkpYw0nVfnDddl8Pwtveb0
1790555708129020	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3ox9	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-30vn"}	blake3:e2ic9-_FA3sg0p5edCeN4EkfIym4MiG0IlMw324_bDc
1790555708295860	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-285u	{"description":"Found by the managed-section audit. Contradicts the managed section's rules:\n- worker-loop.md and finish.md have the worker run a bare `maw ws merge` on reviewed work, skipping `edict protocol merge` (review log commit, clean check, risk:critical gate).\n- They then run `maw push`, but workers must not push; the lead merges and pushes.\n- worker-loop.md around L143 has a general review done by a subagent with no check of the Seal verdict (`seal review <id> --format json`).\n\nFix the docs to route reviewed work through `edict protocol merge`/`finish` steps, drop the worker push, and require the Seal verdict check. Regenerate .agents/edict copies; keep the retarget regression test green.","kind":"bug","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"worker-loop.md/finish.md: bare maw ws merge on reviewed work, worker pushes, subagent review without Seal verdict check"}	blake3:C0Y4Dw3fa14fziB1PngO4yCKhXIHOLeopwTfxIev1dU
1790555708351790	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3ox9	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-285u"}	blake3:oECNK8_rVvxvwrRj8y9G4WOmA8aEEh0bKB_ofej7ERU
1790555708522209	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-14gy	{"description":"Found by the managed-section audit. src/commands/dev_loop/prompt.rs says around L495 that the merge 'may miss uncommitted' changes and around L523 that it takes them. The audit confirmed in a sandbox that `maw ws merge` silently merges uncommitted edits, deletions and untracked files. Make both passages say that, and point at the clean check the protocol merge step runs. Test on the built prompt.","kind":"bug","labels":["docs"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"xs","title":"Dev-loop prompt contradicts itself about maw ws merge and uncommitted changes"}	blake3:Ydc-PzF6lLAPbIzDm5z1iHbJsjGF-bEfePPycn30bOs
1790555708583136	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3ox9	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-14gy"}	blake3:xoIADIo2MsxblOrURWQwFqzXCaTL4Z5WRCCv6nfqUqM
1790555708749530	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1l2w	{"description":"Found by the managed-section audit. In the root layout, bn runs directly at the repo root (the managed section says so), but edict protocol output always prints `maw exec default -- bn ...`, the bare-layout form. Use the layout-aware bn prefix the templates already have (`{{ bn }}` / Layout) in protocol output too. Tests: protocol start/finish output for a root-layout project has no `maw exec default -- bn`; bare layout keeps it.","kind":"bug","labels":["cli"],"parent":"bn-30a0","size":"s","title":"Protocol output uses bare-layout 'maw exec default -- bn' in root-layout projects"}	blake3:TtLuBlWU3p5Xqq3WkLAkSuiQNF0CSm0OJXkslndCmrk
1790555708805125	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-21zp	{"body":"From the audit (notes/managed-trim-audit.md): (1) remove/fix false claims: 'maw ws merge auto-syncs stale sources' (false: it refuses a stale source), 'bypass with --force' (a second marker check cannot be bypassed), 'maw ws create handles branching' (worktrees are detached; maw creates no branches), 'always --check before --destroy' (merge runs the same checks). (2) Template ignores tools/review toggles: gate the seal/rite/maw bullets on config.tools. (3) Docs index is missing coordination.md and mission.md, and groom.md's description is just 'groom'. (4) Tests to update: src/template.rs ~L565-579 assert bones-table strings; ~L621 asserts '## Edict Workflow'. (5) Rules list: start from the audit's 12-bullet draft plus 'Confirm before destructive actions' (kept from the dropped Replies-to-a-human section). (6) Header line: these rules win over tool quick-starts."}	blake3:nuCocEK15HIY3E_t7aW4Z0m61rFrReXHznMjs1fUe8U
1790555708850002	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3ox9	{"body":"From the audit: template and security-review.md disagree on who sends review-done (security-review.md: the author sends it; the dedicated reviewer sends no Rite messages). security-review.md is the source of truth; make every doc agree. Batch anchor rule (LAST id in RITE_BATCH_MESSAGE_IDS) verified in rite src/cli/hooks.rs; document it in cross-channel.md or the Rules list, not both."}	blake3:j9WYSO4ZSx1AS-As9UJZk974q_MUsNfrW6E7z6x6OWw
1790555727212157	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-30a0	{"body":"Upstream tool-doc bones filed from the audit: maw bn-39nsp, rite bn-2h2d, seal bn-3j7p. The trimmed section points at these tools' own docs, so until they land, the Rules list must carry the correct form of anything they get wrong (anchored ask-and-wait, maw exec for seal, mark-merged ordering, edict merge path)."}	blake3:vmXpSDvfjY1oSJt4oKXIf0BWGeGkuup5kAguWlP61QY
