1790557075901477	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-61kf	{"description":"Found while building the eval harness (bn-1oug, evals/scripts/lib/common.sh). vessel ignores XDG_RUNTIME_DIR for its socket, and its server re-execs into the fixed systemd unit `vessel-server.scope`. So with RITE_DATA_DIR/HOME/XDG_* sandboxed as AGENTS.md 'Testing template changes safely' says, a sandbox rite hook that fires runs `vessel spawn` against the REAL vessel server. During harness probing a sandbox responder hook did exactly that (it skipped a self-message and exited without a model call).\n\nFix: add VESSEL_SOCKET (pointing inside the sandbox) to the recipe and to the hermetic tests' env helpers, and document the systemd-run re-exec issue (the harness shims systemd-run to fail). Cross-check tests/hermetic_rite_hooks.rs, tests/sync_dry_run.rs, tests/init_dry_run.rs, tests/rite_hook_guard_refuses_live_hooks.rs, tests/dry_run_refuses_live_hooks.rs. Upstream vessel issue filed separately. Acceptance: with the recipe's env, `vessel list` and `vessel spawn` talk to a sandbox server (or fail), never the real one; verify with a real vessel list before/after.","kind":"bug","labels":["rite","docs"],"size":"s","title":"Sandbox recipe does not isolate vessel: a sandboxed hook can spawn into the real vessel server","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:PBdItnazbn4fMLpHIx1IGeTUwm9lN7m7629v6y6xc_c
1790557077236861	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2cyu	{"description":"Found by the eval harness (bn-1oug): maw workspaces run on a detached HEAD, and seal 0.30 then reported `approval_stale:false` and `mark-merged` accepted a commit made after the LGTM. `edict protocol merge` (src/commands/protocol/merge.rs, freshness via `seal diff --format json`) relies on approval_stale, so a post-LGTM code commit merges unreviewed. Upstream seal issue filed separately.\n\nFix in edict (defense in depth, keep after seal is fixed): also compare seal's `approved_commit` with the workspace HEAD (the fallback `freshness_from_summary` already does something similar for older seal); if they differ and the difference touches anything outside `.seal/reviews/<id>/`, treat the approval as stale. Tests with a fake seal JSON where approval_stale=false but approved_commit != HEAD.","kind":"bug","labels":["review"],"size":"s","title":"protocol merge trusts seal approval_stale, which misses post-LGTM commits in detached-HEAD maw workspaces","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:wl5rPiAkZl1NnvglYeTctPybM6hnA2jizgXskdzIETU
1790557078550480	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-25cq	{"description":"Found by the eval harness (bn-1oug): `edict protocol finish` and `merge` print `rite send --agent agent ...` and `rite claims release --agent agent ...` rather than the real agent name. Sonnet corrected it on its own, but a weaker model would send as 'agent'. Find where the placeholder leaks (likely a default or a literal in src/commands/protocol/*), use the --agent value, and add a test that protocol output never contains `--agent agent`.","kind":"bug","labels":["cli"],"size":"xs","title":"edict protocol finish/merge print '--agent agent' instead of the agent name"}	blake3:myxTjhNOozJlEgCq5L-4fSqTqIpWqRO16ln3IUiSzVo
1790557079496953	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2qkz	{"description":"Found by the eval harness (bn-1oug): non-interactive init with bones enabled leaves no .bones/ (init_bones defaults to false without prompts; the harness runs `bn init` itself). A project that enables bones should get it initialised; keep --no-init-bones as the opt-out. Check seed_work defaults the same way. Test in the sandboxed init tests (tests/init_dry_run.rs pattern): --tools bones --no-interactive creates .bones/, and the dry-run plan lists `bn init`.","kind":"bug","labels":["cli"],"size":"xs","title":"edict init --no-interactive --tools bones skips bn init"}	blake3:6RZ8kwHcfm0hpftk9ACcnv9ax7IWaabZU8pojrfwxMg
