1790565702069794	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-30a0	{"body":"A/B verdict (evals/results/2026-09-27-managed-ab-summary.md, 0db3b600): 18 interleaved runs, one edict build, only the managed block differed (~5,068 vs ~1,327 tokens). Mean scores trimmed vs baseline: worker 135.0 vs 133.3/135, review-loop 185.0 vs 181.7/185, lead-merge 106.7 vs 103.3/110. Failures: trimmed 1 (L7x1), baseline 5 (W14x1, R5x2, L7x2). L7 is a scaffold gap (Cargo.lock not gitignored); R5/W14 read as model variance, not trim-caused. No regression; n=3 so supportive, not conclusive. Safety checks clean in all runs; cost ~$11.2."}	blake3:53oz-OnG7O7IRHh60ZCSlGQxENAmbTGeYECcf44cLNE
1790565702213016	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-34bm	{"description":"From the managed-section A/B (evals/results/2026-09-27-managed-ab-summary.md): the lead runs cargo test at the project root after merging, which leaves an untracked Cargo.lock, and L7 (clean root) fails. Harness gap, seen under both variants. Gitignore Cargo.lock (or target/ and Cargo.lock) in the greeter scaffold, or exclude build artifacts from the W3/L7 checks. Selftest must stay green.","kind":"task","labels":["evals"],"size":"xs","title":"Eval scaffold: gitignore Cargo.lock so a post-merge cargo test does not trip L7"}	blake3:j3S59dA2rmOyEFyzAse54QP5kralUy0u3wK1bmZqb-M
